      "disposition": "shared_derived_raw_field_contract",
      "assessment": "All three sites already call the same UsageEnvelope function and append the reported-total field. Ledger CounterPolicy tracks it, Record persists/validates it, and Aggregate.Key retains a separate token measure. This is a six-field raw observation contract, not the five billable/reconciled dimensions. A separately named raw_fields API could own the derivation; do not price reported_total as another additive dimension or delete it.",
