      "disposition": "shared_unsigned_storage_bound",
      "assessment": "Five attribute sites and a sixth inline UsageAggregate.Checkpoint bounded/1 use the same unsigned-64 ceiling. These are storage-domain bounds, not operational timeouts. Keep positive positions separate from nonnegative counters/generations and preserve error envelopes. Record.bounded_integer?/1 is already reused by CounterPolicy and Ledger.Checkpoint; a storage leaf could centralize the primitive without coupling aggregate decoding to the full ledger record implementation.",
      "related_finding": "telemetry-usage-22",
      "extra_sites": [
        {
          "path": "src/lib/aiur/usage_aggregate/checkpoint.ex",
          "line": 167
        }
      ],
      "caveat": "RetiredFloor.write/3 checks nonnegative integers but does not apply the ceiling in its visible guard/body, while its loader does. Equality of decoder constants does not prove every writer is symmetrically bounded. Caller reachability and runtime effect of an oversized floor were not investigated; do not present a reproduced incident."
    }
